M4.23 pre-install backup Google Drive quota diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28

Error image
-----------
The fresh absent-state backup reached ten low-level upload repetitions before
rclone recorded whole-operation attempt 1/3 as failed. Google Drive returned
HTTP 403 `RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` for the project's request-per-minute quota.

Cause
-----
The encrypted remote backend exceeded a Google Drive API request quota while
finalizing the uploaded object. The local archive and server service remained
intact. rclone automatically entered its configured whole-operation retry
sequence and continued with attempt 2/3.

Risk
----
The new archive cannot be accepted as remote backup evidence until the backup
service exits successfully and an independent remote stream hash matches the
local archive hash. No installation, ACL, PostgreSQL, identity, release or
systemd mutation has begun.

Rollback
--------
No installation rollback is required because the installation boundary was
not crossed. Do not terminate the active rclone retry unless it becomes stuck
without its own bounded retry result. A final failed service leaves the prior
verified archive as historical evidence but does not authorize installation.

Approved continuation
---------------------
Allow the existing bounded rclone attempt 2/3 and, if needed, 3/3 to finish.
Continue only on service result success, zero exit status, one exact remote
object, matching local/remote SHA-256 and a successful non-disruptive restore
smoke. Any final failure keeps M4.23 at NO-GO.
